Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• USERS."created_at": filter users who signed‑up between 2019‑01‑01 (1546300800000000) and 2022‑04‑30 (1651363199000000)  
• USERS."gender": separate cohorts (Male / Female).  
• USERS."age": find minimum & maximum ages inside the date‑window and count users at those ages.  
• USERS."id": unique identifier for counting rows (users).  

Typical conditions you will reuse  

WHERE  
    "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000  
    AND "gender" IN ('M','F')  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL snippets, progressing from simple exploration to the final aggregated answer.  
Every column name is enclosed in double quotes; each query is annotated and capped with LIMIT 20 when practical.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a handful of users who signed up in the required window.
SELECT *
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show distinct genders found within the time window.
SELECT DISTINCT "gender"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Display distinct ages for female users in the window (sample).
SELECT DISTINCT "age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "gender" = 'F'
  AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
ORDER BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Display distinct ages for male users in the window (sample).
SELECT DISTINCT "age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "gender" = 'M'
  AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
ORDER BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Retrieve the minimum and maximum ages per gender (no counts yet).
SELECT
    "gender",
    MIN("age") AS "min_age",
    MAX("age") AS "max_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
  AND "gender" IN ('M','F')
GROUP BY "gender"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Count how many users are at each age for females (sample list).
SELECT
    "age",
    COUNT(*) AS "female_user_count"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "gender" = 'F'
  AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY "age"
ORDER BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Count how many users are at each age for males (sample list).
SELECT
    "age",
    COUNT(*) AS "male_user_count"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "gender" = 'M'
  AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY "age"
ORDER BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Female cohort – get counts for both min and max age in one shot.
WITH female_stats AS (
    SELECT MIN("age") AS "min_age", MAX("age") AS "max_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "gender" = 'F'
      AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
)
SELECT
    u."age",
    COUNT(*) AS "female_user_count"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN female_stats fs
      ON u."age" IN (fs."min_age", fs."max_age")
WHERE u."gender" = 'F'
  AND u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY u."age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Male cohort – counts for both min and max age in one shot.
WITH male_stats AS (
    SELECT MIN("age") AS "min_age", MAX("age") AS "max_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "gender" = 'M'
      AND "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
)
SELECT
    u."age",
    COUNT(*) AS "male_user_count"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN male_stats ms
      ON u."age" IN (ms."min_age", ms."max_age")
WHERE u."gender" = 'M'
  AND u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY u."age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final answer – for each gender, show min_age, users_at_min_age, max_age, users_at_max_age.
WITH age_bounds AS (
    SELECT
        "gender",
        MIN("age") AS "min_age",
        MAX("age") AS "max_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
      AND "gender" IN ('M','F')
    GROUP BY "gender"
)
SELECT
    ab."gender",
    ab."min_age",
    SUM(CASE WHEN u."age" = ab."min_age" THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "users_at_min_age",
    ab."max_age",
    SUM(CASE WHEN u."age" = ab."max_age" THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "users_at_max_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN age_bounds ab
     ON u."gender" = ab."gender"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY
    ab."gender",
    ab."min_age",
    ab."max_age"
LIMIT 20;
```
